      "content": "a measure of tin (worth £2 10s) | raw Cornish tin in large rectangular blocks weighing roughly 200-300 lb. (see also stannum) | tin of second quality cast into blocks; solid tin as distinct from tin plate (OED s.v. tin n. 1b) | a packing unit for box wood of no particular size"
